From: mscharged-port
Subject: Competitive play: a Recharged set plays fair ball contests by its rules
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Feder's fair ball contests (0023) are on in every online match, so that
both machines update the players in the same order. The profile server's
rules now say whether a set plays with them (the rule fair_ball_contests):
a challenge's or a tournament set's game (mscharged_competitive_set_game)
plays with them only when its rules have them, whatever either player
chose for their own games; both machines have the set's rules, so they
still agree. A replay of such a game plays by the set's tweaks it recorded.
Every other online match, and offline play, stays as it was.

diff --git a/src/Game/Game.cpp b/src/Game/Game.cpp
index 4feea13..24fec85 100644
--- a/src/Game/Game.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Game.cpp
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@
 #include "mscharged_tweaks.h"
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
 #include "Game/DB/CharacterInfo.h"
+#include "mscharged_competitive.h"
 #endif
 #include "Game/Render/ElectricFence.h"
 #include "Game/ReplayChoreo.h"
@@ -1465,9 +1466,13 @@ void cGame::PreUpdate(float deltaTime)
 // Port tweak "Feder's fair ball contests": every step updates the defending
 // team's players first, each team in an order shuffled without bias. Online
 // matches always play with it, so that both machines update the players in
-// the same order.
+// the same order. Tweak patch 0083: a Recharged set's game, and its replay,
+// plays with it only when the set's rules have it, whatever either player
+// chose (both machines have the same rules).
 static bool FairBallContests()
 {
+    if (mscharged_competitive_tweak(MSCHARGED_TWEAK_FAIR_BALL_CONTESTS)) return true;
+    if (mscharged_competitive_set_game()) return false;
     return mscharged_tweak_enabled(MSCHARGED_TWEAK_FAIR_BALL_CONTESTS) || GameInfoManager::Instance()->IsOnline();
 }
 
